window.docContents[201].resolve({"/#Cvc___lean----High-Level-CVC5-API":{"contents":"Cvc.lean is a high-level Lean 4 API for the cvc5 SMT solver, built on top of the\nlean-cvc5 Lean library. It adds a lot of quality of life features and strives to\nprovide strong static guarantees. The following section of this manual present the library in\ndetails. The rest of this introduction illustrates what using cvc.lean looks like in practice.\n\n\n\nTyped terms and solver creation.\n\nopen Typed in\ndef setup : Env (Solver × Term Bool × Term Int) := do\n  let solver ← Solver.new\n  solver.setOption \"produce-models\" \"true\"\n  let b1 ← Term.mkSymbol \"b1\"\n  let i1 ← Term.mkSymbolAs Int \"i1\"\n  let formula ← smt! ¬ b1 ∨ (b1 ∧ 0 < i1)\n  solver.assert formula\n  return (solver, b1, i1)\n\n\nSimple check-sat.\n\n#eval Env.runIO do\n  let (solver, b1, i1) ← setup\n  println! \"check-sat\"\n  solver.checkSat\n    (ifSat := do\n      let b1 ← solver.getValue b1\n      let i1 ← solver.getValue i1\n      println! \"-sat: b1 ↦ {b1}, i1 ↦ {i1}\")\n\n\ncheck-sat\n-sat: b1 ↦ false, i1 ↦ 0\n\n\nopen Typed in\n#eval Env.runIO do\n  let (solver, b1, i1) ← setup\n  println! \"check-sat assuming {b1}\"\n  solver.checkSat (assuming := #[b1])\n    (ifSat := do\n      let b1 ← solver.getValue b1\n      let i1 ← solver.getValue i1\n      println! \"- sat: b1 := {b1}, i1 := {i1}\")\n\n  let i1_eq_zero ← smt! i1 = 0\n  println! \"check-sat assuming {b1} and {i1_eq_zero}\"\n  solver.checkSat (assuming := #[b1, i1_eq_zero])\n    (ifSat := println! \"- sat, unexpected!\")\n    (ifUnsat := println! \"- unsat\")\n    (ifUnknown := fun reason =>\n      println! \"- solver could not decide 😥:\\n  {reason}\")\n\n\ncheck-sat assuming b1\n- sat: b1 := true, i1 := 1\ncheck-sat assuming b1 and (= i1 0)\n- unsat\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n","context":"","header":"Cvc.lean -- High-Level CVC5 API","id":"/#Cvc___lean----High-Level-CVC5-API"}});